  "details": "I've been having a recurring VR Chat bug in the Quest version.\n\nI play on a Quest 3S, and recently this bug has been bothering me a lot because it directly affects gameplay!\n\nIt seems like the character simply starts walking on its own, as if the controller has stick drift. When this happens, I'm also unable to open menus or interact with objects.\n\nThe only way to fix the problem is to open the goal menu and then close it immediately.\n\nIt works just fine on other games and there is no stick drift on the controllers.\n\nAnd thinking better, if was something wrong with the controllers, I still should be able to open the menus and interact with objects around me. Like pickups, buttons... Any kind of interaction object...\n\nI think it's some kind of bug with the mobile feature happening on the quest version of the game.\n\nBecause the mobile version have a setting that allows players to double tap on screen to start walking.\n\nMAYBE it's happening on the quest version for some reason...\n\nBut idk...\n\nIt's just a guess...",
